1
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:06,340
I carry high my craven flag,

2
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:11,277
my ally I'm gonna fly and let my
struggles shoot me through the sky!

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:14,997
It'd be a pity if we
lingered here and let our

4
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:18,057
pretty sparks of life
blend aloud and disappear?

5
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:23,117
There may be fog that even
you can't navigate If someone

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,837
strong like you is lost then
who will set me straight?

7
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,697
Cause when the waves
cast, my heart exists.

8
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,737
It's been your kindness and your strength!

9
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:33,057
That would free me from the mist.

10
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,840
And just like that!

11
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:37,957
We move on.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,537
Sail to a new dawn.

13
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:43,317
Weigh anchor, ride as high as you can!

14
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,437
I assure I don't need anger.

15
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,577
I go fast as I am, yeah.

16
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:50,637
I hear you laughing like
you're numb to it all?

17
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,617
Well, we're dashing together.

18
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,077
No, we're never gonna fall, you know!

19
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:57,617
The whole world may now be my enemy.

20
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:01,580
What a swirl, but I ain't
backing down so long as I'm free!

21
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,157
Thought I'll give it, come
round the current with me.

22
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:09,800
All in, wake up bright and
early, making for the peak we go!

23
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:24,320
All in, wake up bright and
early, making for the peak we go!

24
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,220
A short time ago, before
Luffy's departure,

25
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:43,337
he made a visit to the
ruins of Odin Castle,

26
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:46,773
where the graves of Kozuki
Odin and his allies once were.

27
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:11,000
However, thanks to Kaido's blast breath,
there was nothing left but destruction.

28
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:17,880
Years ago, Odin built his first castle
there when he became the Daimyo of Kuri.

29
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:20,840
I'm the Daimyo!

30
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,070
Luffy!

31
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,390
Hi!

32
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,140
Hello there, Luffy Toto. Hey, guys.

33
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,357
What's going on?

34
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:33,517
Why are all of you here?

35
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,297
We came to tell Lord Odin
that we won the battle.

36
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:40,197
It's been rather eventful since we've
been away, so there's much to discuss.

37
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,809
Bigger question is,
why are you Karoo here?

38
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:44,640
To see Odin, same as you.

39
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:51,517
You two would have been
good friends, I'm certain.

40
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:54,817
He would be honored to meet the man
who saved his country from Kaido!

41
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,440
You think so?

42
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:05,137
Lord Odin, thanks to Sir
Lufitaro and his friends.

43
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,237
We defeated Orochi and Kaido.

44
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:10,160
At long last, the land of Wano is free.

45
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:25,820
As for Lord Momonosuke, he
has become a beloved shogun.

46
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:31,027
With us beside him, he will make this
country a land of peace as it was before.

47
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:32,966
Your people will smile again.

48
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,740
I only wish that Ashura
and Iza were here too.

49
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,897
They'll always be here.

50
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,237
For we will carry them in our hearts.

51
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,400
Just as we do with Lord Oden.

52
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:03,740
Oh, well spoken.

53
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,157
I'm sure they're having their own banquet,

54
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:08,711
and they'll feast again when we join them.

55
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,777
I'm not going to keel over yet,

56
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:14,978
but I can't wait to have
our lord's ode in when I do.

57
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:17,620
I haven't forgotten the flavor.

58
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,240
And how could I?

59
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:21,177
It's the flavor of our friendship.

60
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,297
It tasted even better after training.

61
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:24,620
We ate and ate.

62
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:26,180
That sounds nice.

63
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:28,008
Wish I could try some, too.

64
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:29,570
Yeah, me too.

65
00:04:29,653 --> 00:04:33,188
If you guys know the recipe, we
can have Sanji cook up a pot.

66
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,377
We should stock up on some
ingredients to take on the Sunny.

67
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:38,780
Yeah, go for it.

68
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,861
And get as much as you can carry.

69
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,310
Sir Luffy.

70
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,580
Will you be leaving soon?

71
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,370
Yeah.

72
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:55,080
With all our hearts, once
again, we must thank you.

73
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,360
We owe you our lives.

74
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,440
Cut that out!

75
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:04,640
We're friends, aren't we? Huh?

76
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:07,530
Huh?

77
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:13,140
What's up, Carrot?

78
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,760
You, Chia, can't go!

79
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:16,720
My heart can't take it!

80
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,920
I want to stay with you, Chia!

81
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,400
It's not fair, Nami!

82
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,300
Carrot? What's wrong?

83
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:26,538
Why are you crying?

84
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,240
Because this is goodbye.

85
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:30,520
I'm going back to Zou.

86
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:34,280
I have to protect my homeland
with Wanda and the others.

87
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:43,440
Miyagi, Tristan, thank you for
all your help. My pleasure.

88
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:47,838
Thank you, Karoo, for teaching me
so much as a doctor and as a friend.

89
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:49,497
Please don't work too hard.

90
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:50,462
Get good sleep.

91
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:53,640
Aw, I'm reminded of the first time we met.

92
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:56,117
As I recall, Carrot, you
stowed away on the sunny.

93
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:59,517
Seems your dream to see the
ocean came true in a big way.

94
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,897
Was it all you hoped for?

95
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,720
It was all of that and more!

96
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:07,217
I saw crazy islands and went on big
adventures and made amazing friends!

97
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,980
It was scary sometimes, too.

98
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:12,217
But I think I came out of it
a lot stronger than before.

99
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,780
I owe it all to you, Tia. So thanks!

100
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:20,958
I'll treasure these memories
for the rest of my life!

101
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:25,560
There's only one last thing
for us to do. Got you!

102
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:29,177
I had so much fun spending
time with you, Tia-nami.

103
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:30,340
My Beast.

104
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,680
I miss you.

105
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:34,787
I didn't forget my children.

106
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,480
That tickled carrot.

107
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:38,721
I'm so glad I got to be your bro.

108
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:44,130
Oh, yeah.

109
00:06:44,213 --> 00:06:48,020
When I was coming out here, I
saw Zoro. Yeah? Where was he?

110
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:04,790
20 minutes.

111
00:07:04,873 --> 00:07:05,703
3 minutes.

112
00:07:05,786 --> 00:07:06,616
2 minutes. 2

113
00:07:06,699 --> 00:07:12,880
minutes.

114
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:29,516
Let's share a drink.

115
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,480
What are you doing here?

116
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:47,701
Having a few drinks with
your old man, that's all.

117
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,620
I'll pour one for you!

118
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:52,270
Thanks.

119
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:54,304
Did you put these flowers here?

120
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,290
Huh?

121
00:07:56,373 --> 00:07:57,203
Uh-huh

122
00:07:57,286 --> 00:07:58,116
Big sis helped me out.

123
00:07:58,199 --> 00:07:59,120
It was her idea?

124
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:05,040
Zoro Giri, you came to pay
your respects as well? Yeah.

125
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:31,640
May you rest in peace, Lord Yasui.

126
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,906
They'll build you a nice
temple soon, promise.

127
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:37,957
Then I'll come and visit
you all the time, okay?

128
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:42,000
You'll never be lonely with
me around, Dad. Right? Right!

129
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:54,314
It seems you came here to say farewell.

130
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:56,197
Does that mean you'll be leaving?

131
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,633
That the time has come?

132
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:58,970
Yeah.

133
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,640
I will certainly miss you.

134
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:13,100
Not only you, I will also have to bid
farewell to my father's beloved Enma.

135
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,660
I suppose so.

136
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:23,580
You can't have it back.

137
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:26,057
No, of course not.

138
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:31,380
He still holds a grip on the blade
that slices through the deepest hells.

139
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,740
Odin was one hell of a swordsman.

140
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,420
This sword is a beast.

141
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,617
It would take a true master to tame it.

142
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,737
It sounds like you're being modest.

143
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:46,037
You saved the land of Wano by
wielding that sword yourself.

144
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,620
You're a master just like my father was.

145
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:50,670
No.

146
00:09:50,753 --> 00:09:51,889
I'm still not good enough.

147
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,480
Don't say that.

148
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:56,240
It looks to me like Enma is rejoicing.

149
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:58,793
It's pleased to have a partner like you.

150
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,040
Now get stronger.

151
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,940
Just watch me, Enma.

152
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:14,220
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

153
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:17,677
You trying to pull one over
on me, you cheeky brat?

154
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,240
What was that, boss?

155
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:22,197
Don't tell me there's something
wrong with my repair work.

156
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,817
You're damn right there is.

157
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:24,730
Wanna fight?

158
00:10:24,813 --> 00:10:28,602
Or do you need to get your eyes
checked, you useless old fart bag?

159
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:33,137
You're the one who asked me to double
check your repairs, you cocky little turd.

160
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:38,161
Don't start pissing on me because I did you
a favor, even if it was a waste of time.

161
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,397
Everything's perfect.

162
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,009
But you knew that already.

163
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,000
You little punk.

164
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:44,510
Come on.

165
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,657
You kind of left me a
spot to fix as a courtesy.

166
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:47,570
See?

167
00:10:47,653 --> 00:10:49,237
I climbed up here just
to look like a fool.

168
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:51,920
Sorry you can't handle
my super repair work.

169
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:54,457
You're the shipwright
of the crew, aren't you?

170
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:57,777
The Straw Hats wouldn't have made
it this far if you weren't a pro.

171
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:00,960
So long, you damn oversized blockhead.

172
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:04,960
I gotta miss your big fat mouth.

173
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:06,460
I'll miss you.

174
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:12,240
Is everything OK back there?

175
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:15,480
My apologies, sir. One
moment. I'm on my way.

176
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:18,417
Here, thank you for your patience.

177
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:19,457
No prop.

178
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:22,037
Now, regarding your color, it's blue.

179
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,160
Trust me, you'll look great!

180
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,337
Usuhachi, you're so cool!

181
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:29,037
He's the most handsome man in all of Wano!

182
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,697
Show me a smile.

183
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:34,100
Of course, young madam,
anything for a fan!

184
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:36,377
Oh yeah!

185
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:38,820
Hey, wait, that's not what I need?

186
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:40,897
Aha, you want a little more flair!

187
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:42,997
Well, I've got just the thing!

188
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:45,433
I know you'll turn some heads with this!

189
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,280
He's so Head!

190
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:48,760
Hey, Lady Killer!

191
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,765
I've never seen anyone
wear that color so well!

192
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,580
He's red hot!

193
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:55,450
Hmm...

194
00:11:55,533 --> 00:11:57,434
Be careful not to fall in love with me.

195
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:59,397
Wait a minute, stop distracting me!

196
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,310
Huh?

197
00:12:00,393 --> 00:12:01,924
I just need plain black fabric.

198
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:02,850
Nothing fancy!

199
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,997
I'm gonna need lots and lots though, okay?

200
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:07,220
But that's so terribly plain, sir!

201
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:09,800
A gentleman like you deserves much more!

202
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,784
Thanks, but it's not like that!

203
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:13,860
Don't tell anyone, but...

204
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:17,670
What?

205
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:19,300
I didn't know, sir!

206
00:12:19,980 --> 00:12:23,077
I shall provide you with the
finest that Wano has to offer!

207
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,380
Nice! Thanks, buddy!

208
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:34,530
Good!

209
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:36,662
I think that's enough for today!

210
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,031
Thank you for the lesson!

211
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,660
Sanguro's special Sabo is here!

212
00:12:45,660 --> 00:12:46,490
Delicious.

213
00:12:46,573 --> 00:12:47,997
I can never get enough of this.

214
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:49,139
Perfect as always.

215
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:51,630
Thank you.

216
00:12:51,713 --> 00:12:52,554
So, what do you think?

217
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:53,740
It's amazing.

218
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,908
That's what I like to hear.

219
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,860
Oh, hey, Chouchou.

220
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:00,280
How's it going, pal?

221
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:01,835
Here, you want a pet?

222
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,337
What a cutie.

223
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:06,740
You like that, huh?

224
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:10,140
What's up? You good?

225
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,560
Oh, it's nothing.

226
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:16,877
I just realized I never thanked
you for everything you did for me.

227
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:19,257
You saved my life at Onigashima.

228
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,877
Don't mention it. Okay.

229
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:23,320
It was my pleasure to help you.

230
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:30,000
Will you sell me your Sabo tomorrow too?

231
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,937
And the next day and the day after that.

232
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:38,037
I feel like it gives me
the power to do my best.

233
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,577
You really know how to
flatter a guy, don't you?

234
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:43,020
But I'm afraid I'm leaving soon.

235
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,670
Already?

236
00:13:45,753 --> 00:13:46,583
But I...

237
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,580
Excuse me.

238
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:51,030
Yes?

239
00:13:51,113 --> 00:13:53,197
I don't suppose you could
spare a bowl for me.

240
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,360
Anytime, Robin.

241
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,380
Thanks for stopping by.

242
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:59,337
And make it a hot one,
if you would, please.

243
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,240
Yes, ma 'am. Coming right up.

244
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:04,560
And can I have one, too?

245
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:06,680
Yeah, fine. Hey!

246
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,220
You're working so hard.

247
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:20,277
Here, I brought you a little snack.

248
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,360
I think you've all earned a break.

249
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:25,300
You're the best. Thanks
a bunch. Looks good.

250
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:26,638
Don't mind if I do.

251
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:32,160
That smells great.

252
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:34,500
And it tastes even better, I bet.

253
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:35,917
Sorry for the wait.

254
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,920
I've been so busy. I
understand. It's okay.

255
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,887
Bet it'll be worth the wait.

256
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:43,280
It sure was.

257
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:02,780
I'm grateful for the food.

258
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:14,180
Your red bean soup's the best
thing in the world, Otsudu?

259
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:17,960
Remember, there's rice cakes too!

260
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:28,557
Mmm, love how it's so soft and chewy.

261
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:31,480
Eat up, you can have as
many bowls as you want.

262
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:41,612
Tama, what's the matter?

263
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:46,357
Even though I'm having fun, I
remembered you're gonna leave soon.

264
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:49,020
And then, I got a lump in my throat.

265
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:56,940
First Ace, then you, all
the people I love, leave.

266
00:15:57,300 --> 00:16:01,300
And after what happened to Ace, I'm
afraid I'll never see you again.

267
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:03,560
Don't worry.

268
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:08,520
You gave me rice when you
barely had any for yourself.

269
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:11,480
We're friends.

270
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:13,400
I could never forget you.

271
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:24,620
Me too.

272
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,860
I won't forget you either.

273
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:29,717
You'll all be in my heart
no matter where you go.

274
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:30,630
That's right.

275
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:33,220
Train hard while I'm gone. I will.

276
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,820
Someday, we'll meet again.

277
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,260
Thank you!

278
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:58,700
Thank you so much, big friend!

279
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:04,300
I'll get real strong! You'll see!

280
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:07,700
I'll be a hero like you and Abe someday!

281
00:17:16,620 --> 00:17:19,580
And now, we return to the present.

282
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,400
Hey, Luffy!

283
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:24,160
We can set sail whenever you're ready!

284
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,270
Alright.

285
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:29,717
But are you really sure you
want to leave like this?

286
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,357
We didn't say goodbye
to Momo or to Kinamon.

287
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:34,917
Seems kind of wrong after all
we've been through with them.

288
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,353
She's right, as always.

289
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:37,950
They'll be fine.

290
00:17:38,033 --> 00:17:39,717
If Luffy wants to go, let's go.

291
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:42,077
Why you gotta be such a bastard, Mosshead?

292
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,820
Screw off, curly brows. Hey! What?

293
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,390
Although,

294
00:17:48,473 --> 00:17:50,957
it is a bit of a shame since
we shared so many adventures

295
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:53,917
with those two even before
we came to the land of Wano.

296
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,294
It does feel a bit cold to
silently sail away like this.

297
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:04,860
Well, Luffy, you can make the call.

298
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:11,920
Don't worry, guys.

299
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,500
He'll be here soon.
